  "slug": "neuronal-state-4725",
  "summary": "Single-cell transcriptomic, multiome and imaging workflows now quantify heterogeneity across kidney, neural, endothelial and glioblastoma systems.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is computational resolution of cellular heterogeneity and maturation state in complex tissue models. A comparative framework integrates single-cell and single-nucleus transcriptomes from 11 kidney organoid, assembloid and transplantation studies, benchmarking maturation across models. In endothelial differentiation, regulatory wiring is mapped to identify a role for Hippo mechanosignaling in lineage branching. Organotchi provides an open-source pipeline for brightfield segmentation, ten-feature morphological profiling and longitudinal tracking of neural organoids. scDORI applies deep learning to single-nucleus multiome data from glioblastoma to infer enhancer-driven gene regulatory networks. What is new is the shift from descriptive profiling toward explicit network inference and standardized benchmarking, though the items do not demonstrate cross-system transfer of these methods.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-10"
}
